---
import PublicLaunchShell from "../components/PublicLaunchShell.astro";
---

<PublicLaunchShell
  eyebrow="Individual account"
  title="Sign in as one person, not as an organization."
  summary="This entry point is for personal Shared Auth sessions. Product roles, subscriptions, resources, and tenant membership remain decisions of the application you enter after authentication."
  host="user.ores-shared-auth.com"
>
  <section class="surface">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Personal identity lane.</h2>
      <p>
        Shared Auth can prove identity and assurance. It does not infer access
        from an email domain, provider profile, GitHub organization, or another
        unverified attribute.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="form-layout">
      <aside class="notice">
        <h2>Before continuing</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the exact authentication hostname shown below.</li>
          <li>Never paste a password, token, cookie, private key, or OTP into a support form.</li>
          <li>Confirm the destination application before completing a sign-in ceremony.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
      <article class="form-panel">
        <h2>Authentication gateway</h2>
        <p>
          The gateway owns the sign-in ceremony. This static entry page neither
          receives nor stores credentials, and it sets no session cookie.
        </p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button" href="https://auth.ores-shared-auth.com">Open Shared Auth</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://app.ores-shared-auth.com">Choose another entry</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLaunchShell>
